From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] amvx: walk imported dma-bufs with the DMA page iterator

get_sg_table_npages() and append_sg_table() walked an imported dma-buf's
sg_table with for_each_sg_page() bounded by sgt->nents (the DMA-mapped
entry count) while reading DMA addresses through a cast of the CPU
sg_page_iter to sg_dma_page_iter. That mixes the CPU view (sg->length,
orig_nents) with the DMA view (sg_dma_len, nents). It is harmless only
while the two views coincide, i.e. the VPU sits behind no IOMMU (true on
Sky1 today: CIXH3010:00 has no iommu_group). Behind an IOMMU that merges
segments, nents < orig_nents and the walk maps too few VPU pages (firmware
MMU ABORT); under CONFIG_DMABUF_DEBUG the exporter's mangled CPU view is
what is read. for_each_sgtable_dma_page() + sg_page_iter_dma_address() is
the documented importer API and gives the same result when there is no
IOMMU.

Compile-checked against the r285 7.3.0-rc6-sky1-ncz headers (kernel CFLAGS,
no warnings). NOT runtime-tested (no module loads on the test boards); on
current Sky1 hardware it is behaviour-neutral by construction.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/driver/if/mvx_mmu.c
+++ b/driver/if/mvx_mmu.c
@@ -400,10 +400,11 @@
  */
 static size_t get_sg_table_npages(struct sg_table *sgt)
 {
-    struct sg_page_iter piter;
+    struct sg_dma_page_iter diter;
     size_t count = 0;
 
-    for_each_sg_page(sgt->sgl, &piter, sgt->nents, 0) {
+    /* DMA segments (nents / sg_dma_len), the same view append_sg_table() maps */
+    for_each_sgtable_dma_page(sgt, &diter, 0) {
         count++;
     }
 
@@ -421,7 +422,7 @@
                struct sg_table *sgt)
 {
     size_t count;
-    struct sg_page_iter piter;
+    struct sg_dma_page_iter diter;
 
     count = get_sg_table_npages(sgt) * MVX_PAGES_PER_PAGE;
 
@@ -432,12 +433,11 @@
         return -ENOMEM;
     }
 
-    for_each_sg_page(sgt->sgl, &piter, sgt->nents, 0) {
+    for_each_sgtable_dma_page(sgt, &diter, 0) {
         int j;
         phys_addr_t base;
 
-        base = (phys_addr_t)sg_page_iter_dma_address((struct sg_dma_page_iter *)(&piter)) &
-               PAGE_MASK;
+        base = (phys_addr_t)sg_page_iter_dma_address(&diter) & PAGE_MASK;
 
         for (j = 0; j < MVX_PAGES_PER_PAGE; ++j)
             pages->pages[pages->count++] =
